    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0903" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672/573: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the High Commissioner
                        in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-09T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Department’s 22, March 3, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d754-f1"/> and your
                    25, March 2, 11 a.m. from Angora. Department agrees to release of texts of notes
                    exchanged on February 17. You should arrange with Turkish Government a date for
                    release far enough ahead to enable you to telegraph Department, thereby insuring
                    simultaneous action in this country and in Turkey.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d754-f1" n="43" xml:id="d754-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated that the question of date and circumstances of publication
                    of notes was receiving Department’s careful consideration.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
